### VROS optimization API
###
### Local setup uses the `dev` profile, which bypasses Keycloak entirely.
### Requests below therefore send NO Authorization header: an empty
### `Authorization: Bearer ` value is rejected by Spring as malformed.
###
### For a non-dev profile, get a real token from http/keycloak-auth.http
### (or POST to Keycloak's token endpoint), paste it into @token, and
### uncomment the `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` lines.
###
### @scenarioId = 9 matches the scenario seeded in the local database
### ("Bucharest Sector 1 High-Density Route"). Change it if your DB differs.
###
### IMPORTANT: run "Submit an optimization job" first. Its response handler
### stores the returned jobId in the global variable {{jobId}}, which the
### status/solution requests use. If you run those first, the URL becomes
### /jobs//solution and you get 404/400.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token =
@scenarioId = 9

### Submit an optimization job (ADMIN in prod; open in dev)
# @name submit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "scenarioId": {{scenarioId}}
}

> {%
    client.global.set("jobId", response.body.jobId);
%}

### Job status (uses the jobId returned by the submit request above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs/{{jobId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Solution (409 until COMPLETED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs/{{jobId}}/solution
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List ALL jobs, newest first (find job ids here)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List jobs for a scenario
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs?scenarioId={{scenarioId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List all failed jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs?status=FAILED
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The problem that was sent: the scenario snapshot (deliveries + vehicles)
### The POST body only references it; the worker receives the full snapshot
### in the OptimizationRequestEvent on the Kafka requests topic.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/scenarios/{{scenarioId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
